From 09e808fbf80b8c3b66fd77977885da2e83db3597 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mario St Jr <mariostjr@noctalia.dev>
Date: Sun, 29 Mar 2026 12:17:26 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] feat(input): add touchscreen 3-finger swipe gestures

Add native touchscreen gesture support that replicates the existing
touchpad 3-finger swipe behavior for workspace switching (vertical)
and horizontal view scrolling.

Implementation:
- TouchSwipeGestureTracker: recognizes 3-finger swipe patterns from
  raw touch_down/motion/up events using centroid-based tracking and
  a 16px movement threshold (matching touchpad/GNOME Shell)
- TouchSwipeGrab: smithay TouchGrab that feeds gesture deltas into
  the existing workspace_switch_gesture_* / view_offset_gesture_*
  layout pipeline with is_touchpad=false
- Input wiring: all touch events feed the tracker unconditionally
  (required because smithay creates implicit grabs on first finger),
  with the swipe grab installed when the gesture is recognized

The touchscreen carousel gets the same continuous animation, inertia,
and spring physics as the touchpad gesture.

Closes discussion #463.
